#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""/course-keeper learn with scripted model replies, in four runs, one after another.

Run A (the default vision). Seven turns, every check answers "verdict: none":
turn 1 states a standing instruction, turn 2 states one that /course-keeper forget
then withdraws, turns 3 to 5 are sound, in turn 6 the agent does something that no
check flags (its reply holds the quoted passage across a line break), and turn 7 is
the person's correction, whose answer repeats the agent's words. Then: find without a
hint, cancel, give a hint, accept and test (an alert of today's vision on another
invariant, an earlier turn where both checks alert, exactly the newest 3 earlier turns,
the person's messages up to the tested turn, no standing-instruction list but the
withdrawn one), a new learn that replaces a waiting draft with a quote that is not the
agent's and with no sentence, a sentence that does not start with "Never", already
covered, a new alert on an earlier turn, a quote that only the last turn holds (an
alert of today's vision on an instruction, a silent check with the sentence, one
malformed earlier reply), and never writes or changes the check's state.

Run B (--anti-patterns): a sentence for an existing invariant is offered for that
invariant's section of ANTI-PATTERNS.md, a sentence for a new invariant and one for an
invariant that the vision does not have for VISION.md, a check that alerts on another
invariant with the sentence, malformed replies for every call, every excerpt call
carries the anti-patterns text, and neither file changes.

Run C (--no-vision): /course-keeper learn answers that it needs a vision and calls no model.

Run D: Escape during a learn fork, an excerpt after a /compact that holds its summary, a
compaction ("/rewind", "Summarize from here") that removes the corrected turn, and a
corrected turn too long for the test. In Claude Code 2.1.332 a /compact keeps the earlier
turns in what the plugin reads, so it does not remove the corrected turn.

Not covered: the "already running" guard and the cancel of a learn step in flight.
Claude Code runs a typed slash command only after the previous one has answered, and
Escape aborts the plugin's model calls, so no typed command reaches either path. Tool
rows in an excerpt: the harness starts Claude Code with no tools, so no turn has one.

The scripted learn and excerpt replies prove how the plugin handles a reply. They do
not prove that a real model finds the act or that a sentence works.
"""
